[
  {
    "clave": "ideas.guia.venn",
    "en": "The Venn faces two sets off and what they share falls where they overlap. Pick the region in the bottom bar before adding, or drag an item onto another one and it moves by itself."
  },
  {
    "clave": "ideas.guia.comparacion",
    "en": "The comparison puts two topics in columns and what they share in the middle. It is the Venn as a table: quicker to read when there are many points per side."
  },
  {
    "clave": "ideas.guia.proscontras",
    "en": "Every point weighs from 1 to 5: select it and use − + in the bottom bar. Each column adds up at its foot, so the decision stops being “which list is longer”."
  },
  {
    "clave": "ideas.guia.fuerzas",
    "en": "The force field looks at a change: what pushes it on the left, what holds it back on the right, each with its weight. If the right-hand side wins, go after the heaviest force first."
  },
  {
    "clave": "ideas.guia.foda",
    "en": "Strengths and weaknesses are YOURS; opportunities and threats come from outside. When in doubt, ask yourself whether it depends on you or not."
  },
  {
    "clave": "ideas.guia.eisenhower",
    "en": "Important on top, urgent on the left. The “schedule it” quadrant is the one that moves the needle: if it stays empty, you are firefighting all day."
  },
  {
    "clave": "ideas.guia.decision",
    "en": "Each branch is an option and its consequences hang from it. Write them down even when they seem obvious: what is not written compares to nothing."
  },
  {
    "clave": "ideas.guia.tier",
    "en": "S is the best and D the worst. Whatever you cannot rank yet waits below in “Unranked”: drag it to its row once you are sure."
  },
  {
    "clave": "ideas.guia.ishikawa",
    "en": "The head is the problem and each bone a family of causes (method, equipment, materials, measurement…). Look for CAUSES, not solutions: those come later."
  },
